    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "I fixed the bug in `build.go`, but the tests did not run because the permission prompt blocked `go test`.\n\n**Cause:** Every process wrote to the same temp file, `outDir/page.tmp`. One process could then rename another process's content into its own page.\n\n**Fix:** Each call to `Build` now gets its own temp file from `os.CreateTemp` in `outDir`. It writes the file, forces the data to disk, then renames the file to `name.html`. Different pages publish to different files, so the processes share no file and need no lock. The rename replaces the page in one step, so a reader sees either the old page or the complete new one, never half of one. A failed build deletes its temp file.\n\n**Test:** I added `build_test.go`. It starts 6 separate processes that each publish 50 pages into one directory. It then checks that each page holds its own content and that no temp files are left. Run it with `go test -count=3 ./...`.\n\nNOTE: this relies on no two processes building the same page at once, as you described. If that changes, the last rename wins, but the page is still never mixed or partial.\n\n**TLDR**\nAll processes shared one temp file, `page.tmp`. Now each build uses its own temp file and renames it into place.\nThe new test in `build_test.go` did not run here. Run `go test -count=3 ./...` to check it.",
